t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tFact Sheets\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<li class=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tclass=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-link is-current\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\thref=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/releases/\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\taria-label=\"Releases\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tReleases\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<li class=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tclass=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-link\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\thref=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/remarks/\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\taria-label=\"Remarks\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tRemarks\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<li class=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tclass=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-link\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\thref=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/research/\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\taria-label=\"Research\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tResearch\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</ul>\n\t\t</div>\n\t</nav>\n\t</div>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>President Donald J. Trump returns to South Carolina today to highlight a proven record of results that put workers, families, seniors, and communities first.</strong> Under President Trump and Republican leadership, South Carolinians are seeing historic tax relief, surging private investment and job creation, stronger rural healthcare, and major investments in infrastructure, military readiness, and public safety.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 id=\"h-delivering-tax-relief-for-hardworking-south-carolinians\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Delivering Tax Relief for Hardworking South Carolinians</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>President Trump’s Working Families Tax Cuts are putting real money back in the pockets of Palmetto State workers, families, and seniors.</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>No Tax on Social Security:</strong>&nbsp;Approximately one million South Carolina seniors <a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/South-carolina-WH-OBBB-Savings-by-State.pdf\">benefit</a> from the new senior deduction, with the average senior expected to pay zero federal taxes on Social Security benefits.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Bigger Refunds:</strong>&nbsp;South Carolina taxpayers saw average refunds of <a href=\"https://upgradedpoints.com/news/average-tax-refunds-by-state-county/\">$3,476</a> in 2026.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Protecting Jobs and Wages:</strong>&nbsp;The Working Families Tax Cuts&nbsp;<a href=\"https://nam.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/NAM_Tax_Wins_Collection_Final.pdf#page=42\">safeguarded</a>&nbsp;86,000 South Carolina jobs, $15 billion in state GDP, and $8 billion in workers’ wages.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Opportunity Zones:</strong> In September 2026, Gov. Henry McMaster <a href=\"https://governor.sc.gov/news/2026-09/gov-mcmaster-completes-south-carolinas-opportunity-zone-submission-us-treasury\">submitted</a> South Carolina’s new Opportunity Zone nominations to the Treasury, made possible by the <a href=\"https://home.treasury.gov/news/press-releases/sb0550\">permanent extension</a> of the program — unlocking new private capital and economic opportunity for communities statewide.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 id=\"h-strengthening-rural-healthcare-access\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Strengthening Rural Healthcare Access</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>President Trump is delivering targeted resources to expand access and modernize care in South Carolina’s rural communities.</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Rural Health Transformation:</strong> South Carolina <a href=\"https://www.scdhhs.gov/communications/south-carolina-awarded-200-million-rural-health-transformation-program-funding\">secured</a> $200 million in first-year <a href=\"https://www.cms.gov/newsroom/press-releases/cms-announces-50-billion-awards-strengthen-rural-health-all-50-states\">funding</a> through the Working Families Tax Cuts’ Rural Health Transformation Program.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Modernizing Care Delivery:</strong> In September, the state <a href=\"https://governor.sc.gov/news/2026-09/south-carolina-announces-recipients-rural-health-transformation-program-funding\">awarded</a> $167.3 million in Rural Health Transformation Program grants to 228 rural providers for primary care, maternal care, pediatrics, and behavioral health — removing barriers and building long-term capacity through facility modernization, technology upgrades, and workforce development.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 id=\"h-unleashing-private-investment-and-job-creation\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Unleashing Private Investment and Job Creation</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>President Trump’s pro-growth, America First agenda is driving major private investment and high-quality job creation throughout the Palmetto State.</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>NorthMark Strategies is <a href=\"https://scdailygazette.com/2025/04/22/cutting-edge-supercomputing-facility-a-2-8b-investment-planned-for-spartanburg-county/\">committing</a> $2.8 billion to build a high-performance computing center in Spartanburg.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Octapharma is <a href=\"https://www.octapharma.com/news/press-release/2026/octapharma-to-build-1-5-billion-state-of-the-art-critical-care-manufacturing-facility-in-rock-hill-sc\">investing</a> $1.5 billion to construct a critical care manufacturing facility in Rock Hill.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Ferrara Candy Company is <a href=\"https://www.ferrara.com/us/en/ferrara-candy-company-selects-orangeburg-county-new-manufacturing-site\">investing</a> $675 million to establish its first South Carolina operation in Orangeburg County.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Okonite is <a href=\"https://governor.sc.gov/news/2026-09/okonite-expands-orangeburg-county-operations\">investing</a> $400 million to build a new high-voltage electric cable plant in Orangeburg, creating 105 jobs.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Eaton is <a href=\"https://www.eaton.com/us/en-us/company/news-insights/news-releases/2025/eaton-invests-in-new-south-carolina-transformer-manufacturing.html\">investing</a> $340 million to expand U.S. transformer production in Jonesville.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Scout Motors is <a href=\"https://wach.com/news/local/scout-motors-to-invest-additional-300-million-in-south-carolina-site-facility-investments-supplier-jobs-blythewood-richland-county-manufacturer-cars-electric-vehicles\">investing</a> $300 million to develop a Supplier Park at its Blythewood Production Center and seven of its suppliers are <a href=\"https://www.foxcarolina.com/2026/10/14/scout-motors-name-suppliers-spartanburg-bringing-new-jobs-upstate/\">investing</a> more than $82 million across Spartanburg, Duncan, and Piedmont.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Adeptus USA is <a href=\"https://governor.sc.gov/news/2026-10/adeptus-usa-selects-anderson-county-establish-first-south-carolina-operation\">investing</a> $215.6 million to launch its first South Carolina operation in Anderson County, creating 217 jobs.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>TS Conductor is <a href=\"https://thebusinessdownload.com/ts-conductor-to-open-134m-facility-in-south-carolina-bringing-462-clean-energy-jobs/\">investing</a> $134 million to open an advanced manufacturing facility in Hardeeville.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>AmbioPharm is <a href=\"https://governor.sc.gov/news/2026-06/ambiopharm-expands-aiken-county-operations\">investing</a> $119 million to expand peptide manufacturing and development at its Aiken County facility.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Rolls-Royce is <a href=\"https://www.cnbc.com/2025/07/15/rolls-royce-south-carolina.html\">investing</a> $75 million to expand its Aiken manufacturing facility.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Red Metals is <a href=\"https://governor.sc.gov/news/2026-06/red-metals-establishes-first-copper-manufacturing-operation-charleston-county\">investing</a> $70 million to establish a copper manufacturing operation in Charleston County.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Century Aluminum Co. is <a href=\"https://www.postandcourier.com/business/industry/sc-century-aluminum-tariffs-trump-berkeley-county/article_dc587485-e451-44a9-af47-b0ae50ed01f8.html\">investing</a> $50 million to restore its Berkeley County plant to full capacity for the first time in a decade.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>George Utz Inc. is <a href=\"https://www.plasticstoday.com/packaging/georg-utz-invests-40m-in-south-carolina-facility\">investing</a> $40 million to build its first South Carolina manufacturing facility in Sumter County.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Re:Build is <a href=\"https://governor.sc.gov/news/2026-10/rebuild-expands-york-county-operations\">investing</a> $20 million to open an advanced composites plant for aerospace and defense products in Rock Hill.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Tyson Steel is <a href=\"https://governor.sc.gov/news/2026-09/tyson-steel-selects-pickens-county-first-south-carolina-operation\">investing</a> $15.2 million to establish its first South Carolina operation in Pickens County.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Coastal Precast Systems is <a href=\"https://www.greenvillebusinessmag.com/stories/coastal-precast-systems-announces-laurens-county-operation,29529\">investing</a> $9 million to relocate its operations to Laurens County.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>UFP Packaging is <a href=\"https://www.governor.sc.gov/news/2026-08/ufp-packaging-grows-south-carolina-footprint-new-cherokee-county-operation\">investing</a> $5.3 million to open a wood packaging plant in Gaffney.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 id=\"h-investing-in-south-carolina-communities\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Investing in South Carolina Communities</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>President Trump is delivering targeted federal resources that strengthen roads, military installations, disaster recovery, and educational opportunity.</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Strengthening Roads and Bridges:</strong> In July 2026, the Trump Administration <a href=\"https://www.scdot.org/inside/SCDOTPress/2026/scdot-receives--23-5-million-federal-grant-for-statewide-bridge-.html\">awarded</a> South Carolina a $23.5 million grant to replace 18 aging bridges across nine counties.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Modernizing Military Installations:</strong> The FY 2027 NDAA <a href=\"https://mace.house.gov/media/press-releases/rep-nancy-mace-delivers-major-wins-south-carolina-and-americas-warfighters\">authorized</a> $161.7 million for a nuclear power training facility expansion at Joint Base Charleston and extended funding totaling $166.7 million for new recruit barracks at Parris Island.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Delivering Disaster Recovery:</strong> In October 2026, President Trump <a href=\"https://governor.sc.gov/news/2026-10/gov-mcmaster-announces-approval-federal-cost-share-adjustment-hurricane-helene\">approved</a> South Carolina’s request to raise the federal share of Hurricane Helene Public Assistance recovery costs from 75% to 90%.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Supporting HBCUs:</strong> In September 2026, the Trump Administration <a href=\"https://www.scott.senate.gov/media-center/press-releases/sen-tim-scott-applauds-u-s-department-of-education-investment-in-south-carolinas-hbcus/\">awarded</a> nearly $10 million to eight South Carolina HBCUs, led by $2.4 million to South Carolina State.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 id=\"h-making-south-carolina-safe-again\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Making South Carolina Safe Again</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>President Trump and Republicans are delivering results that reduce crime and restore safety for South Carolina families.</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Violent crime <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/FBIColumbiaSC/posts/new-uniform-crime-reporting-numbers-from-2025-show-big-drops-in-crime-across-the/122342895632011761/\">fell</a> 11% and property crime <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/FBIColumbiaSC/posts/new-uniform-crime-reporting-numbers-from-2025-show-big-drops-in-crime-across-the/122342895632011761/\">fell</a> 14% last year, including sharp drops in murders (17%), robberies (19%), aggravated assaults (9%), and burglaries (15%).</li>\n\n\n\n<li>In Charleston, overall crime <a href=\"https://www.charleston-sc.gov/m/newsflash/Home/Detail/1625#docaccess-715460d05e8a64c9d72630e9c62bcc35c160e32391a9a017b640acf4568d3f77\">plunged</a> 36% in 2025, with homicides <a href=\"https://www.charleston-sc.gov/m/newsflash/Home/Detail/1625#docaccess-715460d05e8a64c9d72630e9c62bcc35c160e32391a9a017b640acf4568d3f77\">down</a> 29%, aggravated assaults down 16%, robberies down 24%, and sex offenses down 39% from the five-year average.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>At least <a href=\"https://www.ice.gov/identify-and-arrest/287g#:~:text=287(g)%20Participating,g)%20Participating%20Agencies\">72 law enforcement agencies</a>, including the South Carolina Law Enforcement Division and the South Carolina Department of Public Safety, have signed <a href=\"https://www.ice.gov/identify-and-arrest/287g\">287(g) agreements</a> with ICE to identify, detain, and remove violent illegal alien criminals from the state.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\" />\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>President Trump and Republicans are delivering lower taxes, major private investment, stronger rural healthcare, critical infrastructure, and safer communities.</strong> South Carolinians face a clear choice: continue this progress, or return to the higher taxes, open borders, and failed policies of the past.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/releases/2026/10/president-trump-secures-major-wins-for-south-carolina-workers-families-and-communities/\">President Trump Secures Major Wins for South Carolina Workers, Families, and Communities</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov\">The White House</a>.</p>",
